The HSK 63A Faemat spindle requires a toolholder in the spindle and the chiller to be set at 20°C while the 
spindle is running.
The spindle should be checked periodically for spindle temperature rise. If the temperature rises above 150°F, 
start the program from the beginning.  If the temperature rises above 150°F again, contact your dealer.
SPINDLE WARM-UP PROGRAM
All spindles which have been idle for more than 4 days must be thermally cycled prior to operation above 
6,000 RPM.  This will prevent possible overheating of the spindle due to settling of lubrication.  A 20-minute 
warm-up program has been supplied with the machine, which will bring the spindle up to speed slowly and 
allow the spindle to thermally stabilize.  This program may also be used daily for spindle warm-up prior to 
high-speed use.  The program number is O02020 (Spindle Warm-Up).
